      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "The left septal fascicular block (LSFB) or blockage of the middle fibers of the left bundle branch is probably caused mainly by - in the developed world - the proximal obstruction of the left anterior descending artery (LAD) before its first anterior septal perforator branch (S1). The association of transient LSFB and left anterior fascicular block (LAFB) - left bifascicular block - and the electrocardiographic type 1 Brugada pattern (BrP) has not been described in the literature yet."
      },
